From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wined3d: the backup window gets its own pixel format

When the window's pixel format has been taken by the program's own OpenGL, wined3d falls back to its backup window. It kept the flag that said its format was set through wglSetPixelFormatWINE on the window, took the backup window (no format yet) for one that had it, made no GL drawable for it, and wglMakeCurrent failed: every draw after that failed, Lock returned no memory and Sweet Home 3D (Java 3D and Java2D on one window) faulted in its window procedures hundreds of times. The flag is cleared for the backup window.
---
--- a/dlls/wined3d/context_gl.c
+++ b/dlls/wined3d/context_gl.c
@@ -1327,6 +1327,12 @@
         TRACE("Using backup DC %p.\n", context_gl->dc);
         context_gl->dc_is_private = TRUE;
         context_gl->dc_has_format = FALSE;
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_BACKUP_KEEPS_FORMAT_FLAG
+        /* (wine-sg 8294) the format set through wglSetPixelFormatWINE was on the window's DC: the backup
+         * window has none yet.  With the flag kept, a backup window without a format (wglGetPixelFormat 0)
+         * was taken as already set, no GL drawable was made for it and wglMakeCurrent failed. */
+        context_gl->internal_format_set = 0;
+#endif
 
         if (!wined3d_context_gl_set_pixel_format(context_gl))
         {
